{"pointer": "/scope_contracts/0/bidirectional_evidence/fact_consumer_chain/producer_context", "value": "Charge starts at 2. Normal round-tail processing can reduce it to 1. Reaching the end-of-action cleanup clears exactly count 1 before later Instruct/Dancer processing; count 2 is not cleared by that action cleanup. The clear is not conditional on having used an Electric move or on successfully dealing damage."}
{"pointer": "/scope_contracts/0/bidirectional_evidence/fact_consumer_chain/state_observation_and_later_result", "value": "Charge succeeds in round n: counter 2, then full round-tail 1. In round n+1 the user performs its normal Electric move: its initial damage reads positive Charge and receives the Charge power multiplier. The normal action end clears counter 1 to 0. A later ally’s Instruct repeats that Electric move in the same round, so the repeat reads 0 and receives no Charge multiplier. A timer-only implementation inferred from WP44 keeps 1 through both actions until the round tail and boosts the repeat incorrectly."}
{"pointer": "/scope_contracts/0/bidirectional_evidence/fact_consumer_chain/consumer", "exact_same_value_as": "review/remediation-sixth-20261014-prepare/contracts/R6-U05.json#/scope_contracts/0/bidirectional_evidence/necessary_consumers"}
{"pointer": "/scope_contracts/0/bidirectional_evidence/fact_consumer_chain/definition_vs_wiring", "value": "仅按本记录的具体前提与实际consumer定位；不由名称存在推默认接线。"}
{"pointer": "/scope_contracts/0/premises_and_counterexample/input_domain/0", "value": "Default Charge was successfully used; no special ability/item/state callbacks alter the counter."}
{"pointer": "/scope_contracts/0/premises_and_counterexample/input_domain/1", "value": "Both sides remain able to battle; a later ordinary move attempt reaches its normal end-of-action cleanup."}
{"pointer": "/scope_contracts/0/premises_and_counterexample/input_domain/2", "value": "For the repeat example: a legal positive-PP ordinary Electric move is in the user’s current slots, normal gates pass, and a later ally uses legal Instruct after the user’s ordinary action; no special blacklist, locks, switching, fainting or host fault applies."}
{"pointer": "/scope_contracts/0/premises_and_counterexample/ordinary_control", "value": "Immediately after newly setting Charge to 2, reaching that same action’s end leaves it 2; this is distinct from the count-1 clear. Another independent control removes Instruct and still observes the counter clear after the ordinary action."}
{"pointer": "/scope_contracts/0/premises_and_counterexample/minimal_counterexample", "exact_same_value_as": "review/remediation-sixth-20261014-prepare/contracts/R6-U05.json#/scope_contracts/0/bidirectional_evidence/fact_consumer_chain/state_observation_and_later_result"}
{"pointer": "/scope_contracts/0/premises_and_counterexample/failure_cancel_partial_commit/cancellation_or_partial_commitment", "value": "Successful first damage, PP and history stay committed; a later repeat does not undo them. A failed ordinary attempt that reaches the same end cleanup also clears the remaining count. A fault or branch that does not reach the cleanup has no automatic clear guarantee."}
